`coverage gate` on a two-crate workspace (coverage.in/): each crate against its
gate from the policy, a pending crate listed, and a loosening refused.

```console
$ xtask coverage gate --metadata metadata.json --policy policy.toml --report passing.json
## Rust line coverage per crate

| Crate | Lines covered | Coverage | Gate | Result |
|-------|--------------:|---------:|-----:|--------|
| `cli` |  |  | 90% | pending: UC-3.3 (#825) creates it |
| `core` | 81 / 100 | 81.00% | 80% | pass |
| `schema` | 45 / 50 | 90.00% | 90% | pass |
| **workspace** | 126 / 150 | 84.00% | | |

Every crate meets its gate.

$ xtask coverage gate --metadata metadata.json --policy policy.toml --report failing.json
? 1
## Rust line coverage per crate

| Crate | Lines covered | Coverage | Gate | Result |
|-------|--------------:|---------:|-----:|--------|
| `cli` |  |  | 90% | pending: UC-3.3 (#825) creates it |
| `core` | 81 / 100 | 81.00% | 80% | pass |
| `schema` | 44 / 50 | 88.00% | 90% | **fail** |
| **workspace** | 125 / 150 | 83.33% | | |

error: `schema` is below its gate of 90% lines

$ xtask coverage gate --metadata metadata.json --policy loose.toml --report passing.json
? 1
error: `core` has a gate of 70%, below the default of 80%: the policy never loosens a crate's gate
coverage: 1 error(s) in the policy (loose.toml)

$ xtask coverage gate --metadata metadata.json --policy policy.toml
? 2
xtask coverage: --report FILE is required

$ xtask coverage report
? 2
xtask coverage: expected `coverage gate`
...

```
